622 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (N50:  This is the length of the shortest contig in the assembly such that the sum of lengths of this contig and all longer contigs covers 50% of the total assembly length. It's a measure of the assembly's contiguity, with a higher N50 indicating a better assembly.)
/E (N50:  This is the length of the shortest contig in the assembly such that the sum of lengths of this contig and all longer contigs covers 50% of the total assembly length. It's a measure of the assembly's contiguity, with a higher N50 indicating a better assembly.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
623 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (N90:  Similar to N50, but it represents the length of the shortest contig that covers 90% of the total assembly length. It focuses on the longer contigs that make up most of the assembly.)
/E (N90:  Similar to N50, but it represents the length of the shortest contig that covers 90% of the total assembly length. It focuses on the longer contigs that make up most of the assembly.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
624 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (L50:  This is the minimum number of contigs needed to cover 50% of the total assembly length. A lower L50 indicates a more contiguous assembly because fewer, longer contigs are needed to reach 50% coverage.)
/E (L50:  This is the minimum number of contigs needed to cover 50% of the total assembly length. A lower L50 indicates a more contiguous assembly because fewer, longer contigs are needed to reach 50% coverage.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
625 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
